text='''# Mark 6 — targeted crew shot and group review

Actual text-only reviews by continuity, cinematography, picture editing, Scripture/cultural review, sound and the Production Director are retained with prompts, raw responses and usage. Twelve bounded reasoning requests cover an initial review and owner reconciliation after retrieving the existing spokesperson contract. This is preparation review, not the normal chapter stage’s accepted timed storyboard, audiovisual/native approval or production permission.

All 55 visual beats and eight group quotations were reviewed. Revised instructions preserve crowd arrival/disembarkation, the food check, breaking/giving/distribution order, twelve baskets/five thousand men, intended Bethsaida departure versus Gennesaret landing, retrospective John rebuke, and the disciples’ continuing lack of understanding. Shared banquet exits/eyelines and boat positions are explicit reconstruction proposals. Long instructions have a 16-section source-based picture proposal; actual cast timing is still required. The approved v3 music level is fixed and unchanged.

Preparation casting: existing approved Mark crowd spokesperson for the Nazareth questions and provisionally the first public report; Peter explicitly as production representative for collective disciple lines in 6:35–38 and 6:49. The source still attributes these to groups and does not name Peter as their utterer. No live canon mapping, new voice/performance approval or generated speech follows. The food reply’s isolated endpoint remains held.

**One product choice remains:** three contrasting anonymous reports in 6:14–15. Only one appropriate crowd spokesperson has an approved mapped voice. I recommend retaining all three as original-narrator reported opinions, with separate introductions and nonspeaking context. That needs Dan’s chapter-specific exception to the existing quoted-group voice rule. The standard alternative is two additional reporter voice choices/auditions, using already approved crowd designs. Neither route is silently adopted; see reported-speech-choice.json.

The original blanket proposal to leave all collective dialogue in the narrator voice was withdrawn after policy reconciliation. Offscreen picture alone does not waive character casting. Earlier replies remain evidence, not current decisions. Each owner’s latest findings are preserved in current-findings.json; the Director cannot erase them.

No new Gemini, voice, image or video-generation call, source edit, music change, live DB write or Mark 6 workspace. Reasoning uses the existing Codex allowance/credits route; actual dollars/backend identity are not inferred. The original alignment request ceiling remains exhausted. Full production remains **ON HOLD**.
'''
